{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevHmZhCsHFyLsHKtZs83","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings** — existing code:\n- Shipment model: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt` (line 9-14) defines the data class with `status: ShipmentStatus` enum\n- ShipmentRepository: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt` (line 11-27) provides `save()`, `findById()`, `existsById()`\n- ShipmentController: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt` (line 20-56) has POST, GET endpoints\n- Exception handling: `ApiExceptions.kt` (line 18-24) defines `ResourceNotFoundException` (404), `ConflictException` (409)\n- Error codes: `ApiError.kt` (line 31-37) enum includes `SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`, `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: wraps all `ApiException` instances in the `ApiError` envelope\n\n**Conventions this repository has:**\n- State-changing endpoints return the modified resource via `ResponseEntity`\n- 404 errors use `ResourceNotFoundException` with `ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND`\n- 409 errors use `ConflictException` with a domain-specific error code\n- Error codes are centralized in `ApiError.kt` enum — adding a new code requires one change there\n- Tests use `@SpringBootTest`, `@AutoConfigureMockMvc`, and `MockMvc.perform()` with `jsonPath()` assertions\n- All tests begin with `repository.clear()` to reset state\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ShipmentController.kt` — add confirm endpoint (cannot avoid: endpoint is in the controller)\n2. `ApiError.kt` — add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code (cannot avoid: new error code is required for 409 when shipment is cancelled)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — add tests for confirm (cannot avoid: acceptance criterion 5 requires testing all state transitions)\n\n**Risks:**\n- The confirm endpoint must be truly idempotent: confirming an already-confirmed shipment must succeed and return 200 with unchanged data\n- Confirming a cancelled shipment must reject with 409, not silently succeed\n- Confirming a non-existent shipment must reject with 404, not 409\n- Tests must verify both the idempotency case and the error cases\n\n**Open questions:**\n- None identified that would change the design; the requirement is clear on all cases.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change**, file by file:\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add one error code constant `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the `ErrorCode` enum to signal when a shipment is in a state that prevents the requested operation (e.g., cancelled).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add one new method `confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String)` that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID; if not found, throws `ResourceNotFoundException` (404)\n   - If shipment is already `CONFIRMED`, returns it unchanged with 200 (idempotent success)\n   - If shipment is `CREATED`, transitions it to `CONFIRMED`, saves it, and returns the updated shipment with 200\n   - If shipment is `CANCELLED`, throws `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` (409)\n   - The endpoint is `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` and returns a `ResponseEntity<Shipment>` with status 200\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four new test methods:\n   - `confirms a created shipment` — POST confirm on CREATED should move it to CONFIRMED and return 200\n   - `confirm is idempotent` — POST confirm on already-CONFIRMED should return 200 with no change\n   - `rejects confirm of a cancelled shipment` — POST confirm on CANCELLED should return 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n   - `rejects confirm of a non-existent shipment` — POST confirm on missing ID should return 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\n**Alternative rejected**:\n- Could have added a service layer between controller and repository (e.g., `ShipmentService`) to encapsulate the state transition logic. Rejected because: (a) the existing repository-direct pattern in `OrderController` and `ShipmentController` shows this codebase does not use a service layer, and (b) the Shipment is immutable and the confirm logic is trivial (one if-else chain), so a service class would add ceremony without benefit. Staying with the controller-direct pattern matches the existing architecture.\n\n**Data and error flow**:\n- **Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED)**: Controller calls `findById(shipmentId)` → repository returns `Shipment` → controller creates new `Shipment` with status `CONFIRMED` → calls `save()` → repository updates store → controller returns `ResponseEntity.ok(updated)` (status 200)\n- **Idempotent case (already CONFIRMED)**: Controller calls `findById()` → gets `Shipment` with status `CONFIRMED` → checks status, sees it's already confirmed → returns same instance via `ResponseEntity.ok(shipment)` (status 200, no database change)\n- **Error: not found**: Controller calls `findById(shipmentId)` → repository returns `null` → controller throws `ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)` → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, responds with 404 and `ApiError` envelope\n- **Error: cancelled**: Controller calls `findById()` → gets `Shipment` with status `CANCELLED` → checks status → throws `ConflictException(SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)` → GlobalExceptionHandler catches it, responds with 409 and `ApiError` envelope\n\n**Test strategy**:\n1. **Test: confirms a created shipment** — Setup: create shipment S-1 (will be CREATED) → POST confirm → Assert: 200 OK, status is now CONFIRMED\n2. **Test: confirm is idempotent** — Setup: create S-2, then confirm it once → POST confirm again → Assert: 200 OK, status is still CONFIRMED, no error\n3. **Test: rejects confirm of cancelled shipment** — Setup: directly write CANCELLED shipment to repository (no cancel endpoint exists, so we set it up programmatically) → POST confirm → Assert: 409 Conflict with error code SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n4. **Test: rejects confirm of non-existent shipment** — POST confirm on S-missing → Assert: 404 Not Found with error code SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll write the code."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3282,"cache_read_input_tokens":19110,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3282},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4591477d-d5ca-4e27-976d-e8d4a083a97b","uuid":"28a3f9d1-efb4-496e-b4ee-5506ca533b76","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:12:45.207Z","request_id":"req_011CevHmYSYyPUEfdoWTYHyv"}
