{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevHqNtwaH9ZjvDT4D7Bc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! **Command**: `./mvnw test`\n\n**Result**: BUILD SUCCESS\n\n**Test Summary**:\n- Tests run: 17 (was 13 before)\n- Failures: 0\n- Errors: 0\n- ShipmentControllerTest now shows 9 tests (was 5 before) — the 4 new confirm tests are included\n\nAll tests passed. The new confirm endpoint works correctly:\n- ✅ Confirms a created shipment (CREATED → CONFIRMED)\n- ✅ Confirm is idempotent (re-confirming CONFIRMED returns success)\n- ✅ Rejects confirm of cancelled shipment (409 CONFLICT)\n- ✅ Rejects confirm of non-existent shipment (404 NOT_FOUND)\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping**:\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` succeeded with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 5 original ShipmentControllerTest tests still pass; all 13 original tests across the repo pass\n3. ✅ **POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm confirms and persists** — Implemented in `ShipmentController.confirm()` with `repository.save()`; test `confirms a created shipment` verifies it\n4. ✅ **Error responses consistent** — Uses existing `ResourceNotFoundException` (404) and new `ConflictException` with `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` (409), both handled by `GlobalExceptionHandler` via the standard `ApiError` envelope\n5. ✅ **Repeated confirm succeeds; cancelled rejected; unknown rejected** — Three tests cover these: `confirm is idempotent`, `rejects confirm of a cancelled shipment`, `rejects confirm of a non-existent shipment`\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency** — Only Kotlin/Spring code added; no changes to `pom.xml`\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only these three files touched:\n   - `ShipmentController.kt` — added confirm endpoint (necessary)\n   - `ApiError.kt` — added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` error code (necessary for 409 response on cancelled)\n   - `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — added 4 tests (necessary per acceptance criterion 5)\n\n**Diff review**:\n\n- **ApiError.kt**: Added `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the enum. This is the minimal change needed to introduce the new 409 error case. Placement in the enum is logical (grouped with other SHIPMENT errors).\n\n- **ShipmentController.kt**: \n  - Added `POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm` method with proper routing\n  - Uses `when` expression to handle three status cases cleanly\n  - Returns `ResponseEntity.ok()` for success (both CREATED→CONFIRMED and idempotent CONFIRMED cases)\n  - Throws `ConflictException` for CANCELLED (409)\n  - Throws `ResourceNotFoundException` for missing shipment (404)\n  - Uses immutable `.copy()` to create the updated shipment, consistent with the data class design\n  - No business logic belongs elsewhere; controller directly uses repository as per existing pattern\n\n- **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**:\n  - Added 4 new test methods covering all cases named in the requirement\n  - Uses existing test patterns: `mockMvc.perform()`, `.andExpect()`, `jsonPath()` assertions\n  - One test directly writes to repository to set up CANCELLED state (since no cancel endpoint exists)\n  - Tests verify both happy path (status 200, shipment returned) and error paths (status 409/404, error code in envelope)\n\n**Unresolved findings**: None. All cases the ticket specified are implemented and tested.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add a POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint to transition shipments from CREATED to CONFIRMED status, with idempotent behavior and appropriate 409/404 error responses for invalid states and missing resources.\n\nChanged       \n  - ShipmentController.kt: Added confirm() method with @PostMapping to handle state transitions and error cases\n  - ApiError.kt: Added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE error code for 409 conflict when confirming cancelled shipments\n  - ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 4 new test methods covering all transition paths (CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent, cancelled rejection, not-found rejection)\n\nTests         \n  - confirms a created shipment: POST confirm on CREATED returns 200 OK with status CONFIRMED\n  - confirm is idempotent: POST confirm on already-CONFIRMED returns 200 OK without change\n  - rejects confirm of a cancelled shipment: POST confirm on CANCELLED returns 409 CONFLICT with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE code\n  - rejects confirm of a non-existent shipment: POST confirm on missing ID returns 404 NOT_FOUND with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND code\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS, 17 tests run (4 new), 0 failures\n\nNot done      None. All acceptance criteria met.\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2492,"cache_read_input_tokens":27561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2492},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4591477d-d5ca-4e27-976d-e8d4a083a97b","uuid":"e92d276f-592c-4813-837a-2539d23c3df8","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:13:28.145Z","request_id":"req_011CevHqNAXnQcyNFNUgAmBf"}
